<section image-layout="blank" id="PpUqgwx3Vu" background-color="heading"><grid spacing="none"><grid-item id="YOTeutuW6l" vertical-align="center" colspan="38"><p role="eyebrow">Vietnamese literature · University lecture</p><h1 font-size="40pt">The Tale of Kiều: Nguyễn Du and the Poem That Became a Nation</h1><p font-size="lg">How an inherited plot, a woman's sustained inner voice, and the folk music of lục bát became common cultural property.</p><spacer size="24pt"></spacer><hr color="accent" thickness="md" width="xs"><p font-size="sm">Nguyễn Du · Truyện Kiều · 3,254 lines</p></grid-item><grid-item id="xTQrk1wzvx" padding="0" colspan="22"><img src="https://cdn-staging.gamma.app/QWjS6fBfpt/generated-images/nSKrT1K5reQz0Eo8sVzgq.png" saved-media-id="5xvkaf6e45kxu9o" source="image.ai-generated" fill="true" image-style="vietnamese-manuscript-editorial" alt="Ink-and-opaque-pigment editorial illustration on warm dó-paper-like fibers, an interpretive literary figure seated beside an open manuscript folio and a hồ cầm, a single vermilion thread crossing the page and continuing beyond the frame, lampblack, old gold and indigo under soft window light, Vietnamese chữ Nôm manuscript and woodblock conventions, no legible text or lettering" meta="{&quot;width&quot;:1248,&quot;height&quot;:1664}"></grid-item></grid></section>
<section image-layout="blank" id="TG0KUDIrPq"><grid spacing="none"><grid-item id="j2YBWAr70a"><h2>A country that tells its fortune with a poem</h2><grid spacing="medium"><grid-item id="Ljyn7PvHVY" background-color="accent" vertical-align="center" colspan="20"><display size="lg">3,254</display><h4>lines in chữ Nôm</h4><p>Completed before Nguyễn Du's death in 1820 and carried by recitation as well as reading.</p></grid-item><grid-item id="cga4JKk_d1" colspan="40"><blockquote><p font-size="lg">“So long as The Tale of Kiều survives, our language survives; so long as our language survives, our country survives.”</p></blockquote><p role="caption">Phạm Quỳnh, 1924</p><grid spacing="small"><grid-item id="ugOtFKdejT" cell-style="subtle" colspan="20"><h4>bói Kiều</h4><p>Open the poem at random to divine one's fate.</p></grid-item><grid-item id="E3CDOKg3-8" cell-style="subtle" colspan="20"><h4>lẩy Kiều</h4><p>Quote its lines in a new situation.</p></grid-item><grid-item id="-j0gRxC-Rq" cell-style="subtle" colspan="20"><h4>tập Kiều</h4><p>Recombine its lines into new verse.</p></grid-item></grid></grid-item></grid><p role="caption">Lecture argument: Nguyễn Du inherited a plot, supplied a consciousness, and gave Vietnamese readers a figure through whom history could be read. <a href="https://cand.vn/tieng-tho-lay-dong-dat-troi-post373913.html">CAND</a> · <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Truy%E1%BB%87n_Ki%E1%BB%81u">overview</a></p></grid-item></grid></section>
<section image-layout="blank" id="g5jeug-915" vertical-align="center" background-color="accent"><grid spacing="medium"><grid-item id="STEB21eTY_" vertical-align="center" colspan="18"><display size="lg">I</display></grid-item><grid-item id="V9jbvPM-wE" vertical-align="center" colspan="42"><p role="eyebrow">The life behind the poem</p><h1>The poet</h1><p font-size="lg">Nguyễn Du lived through the end of one political order and served the dynasty that replaced it.</p></grid-item></grid></section>
<section image-layout="blank" id="U8m7yg7Bwv" vertical-align="center"><grid spacing="none"><grid-item id="H57qLh5eOm"><h2 font-size="28pt">He lived through the fall of the Lê, the fall of the Tây Sơn, and the founding of the Nguyễn</h2><grid marker="number" marker-rule="true" marker-position="above" marker-align="start" marker-numbering-format="decimal-leading-zero" spacing="medium" style="--marker-gap: 0.6em;"><grid-item id="Er3pRx29WH" colspan="12"><h4>1765</h4><p>Born in Thăng Long as Nguyễn Du, courtesy name Tố Như.</p></grid-item><grid-item id="41qENLZNUT" colspan="12"><h4>1778</h4><p>Orphaned at thirteen after his parents' deaths and the household's dispersal.</p></grid-item><grid-item id="V4Q_2Eq2FU" colspan="12"><h4>1786–1789</h4><p>Tây Sơn forces take the northern capital; the Later Lê ends in 1789.</p></grid-item><grid-item id="SCfsh3sxZx" colspan="12"><h4>1802</h4><p>The Tây Sơn are defeated and the Nguyễn dynasty is founded.</p></grid-item><grid-item id="26s5SHthd_" colspan="12"><h4>1820</h4><p>He dies eighteen years into the Nguyễn period.</p></grid-item></grid><p role="caption">After 1788 came his “ten years of wind and dust,” poor and without office. Two dynasties fell in his lifetime, not three. <a href="https://scov.gov.vn/dat-nuoc-con-nguoi/nho-danh-nhan-van-hoa-the-gioi-nguyen-du.html">State Committee for Overseas Vietnamese</a></p></grid-item></grid></section>
<section image-layout="blank" id="E5x_ceUdfI"><grid spacing="none"><grid-item id="DqpkK2oyAp"><h2>He took office under the dynasty that replaced the one his family served</h2><grid spacing="medium" vertical-sizing="fill"><grid-item id="TJFjM-67TB" cell-style="subtle" colspan="30"><p role="eyebrow">Documented chronology</p><h3>Service under the Nguyễn</h3><p><b>1802:</b> appointed district magistrate after Gia Long defeated the Tây Sơn. <b>1804:</b> resigned pleading illness, then was recalled and promoted. <b>1813:</b> led a tribute mission to Qing China and returned with <i>Bắc hành tạp lục</i>. He died in <b>1820</b>.</p></grid-item><grid-item id="uFvCnZDanv" cell-style="subtle" colspan="30"><p role="eyebrow">Interpretive limit</p><h3>Keeping faith while surviving</h3><p>The poem's central problem resembles his position: a man raised in Lê service administering for a new house. That resemblance supports a reading of the poem, not a claim about Nguyễn Du's private motives.</p><hr color="accent" thickness="md" width="sm"><p role="caption">The Lê line had already ended in 1789; Gia Long defeated the Tây Sơn in 1802.</p></grid-item></grid></grid-item></grid></section>
<section image-layout="blank" id="rFK_78_AcI" vertical-align="center" background-color="accent"><grid spacing="medium"><grid-item id="qeMc0QFMf5" vertical-align="center" colspan="18"><display size="lg">II</display></grid-item><grid-item id="jJ1ugtHpQL" vertical-align="center" colspan="42"><p role="eyebrow">Source, language, form</p><h1>The making of the poem</h1><p font-size="lg">A Chinese prose romance became a Vietnamese verse narrative organized around interior life.</p></grid-item></grid></section>
<section image-layout="blank" id="JBufKYNIMK" vertical-align="center"><grid spacing="none"><grid-item id="NzTTePOBv_"><h2>What Nguyễn Du did to his Chinese source</h2><grid spacing="medium"><grid-item id="P4PNy0OHRE" cell-style="subtle" colspan="20"><p role="eyebrow">Inherited</p><h3><i>Jin Yun Qiao</i></h3><p>The seventeenth-century prose romance supplied the characters, sequence of events, and moral frame.</p></grid-item><grid-item id="HTb0vfw11o" cell-style="subtle" colspan="20"><p role="eyebrow">Disputed</p><h3>The scale of pruning</h3><p>Đào Duy Anh saw no cutting or addition. Other comparisons find omissions, redistribution, and radical compression. All agree that the plot is inherited.</p></grid-item><grid-item id="FK19tJfMou" background-color="accent" colspan="20"><p role="eyebrow">Transformed</p><h3>Plot becomes psychology</h3><p>The events are borrowed; the sustained interiority is Nguyễn Du's. The reunion alone occupies <b>526 lines</b>, about one sixth of the poem.</p></grid-item></grid><p role="caption"><a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Truy%E1%BB%87n_Ki%E1%BB%81u">Source history and comparative accounts</a></p></grid-item></grid></section>
<section image-layout="blank" id="q8sQ-PnYFG" vertical-align="center"><grid spacing="none"><grid-item id="FKwBdpc1N1"><h2>He also made it Vietnamese, not merely translated</h2><grid marker="number" marker-size="large" marker-style="solid" marker-shape="circle" marker-rule="true" marker-position="above" marker-align="center" marker-straddle="true" spacing="medium"><grid-item id="2tKx3kAFWH" cell-style="outline" colspan="20"><grid-item-label><icon src="https://iconscdn.pictographic.ai/image/7dvsbGkLYjsD3TgdVZ2d.svg?stroke=45" source="image.pictographic.icon" alt="Vietnamese manuscript page and writing brush" meta="{&quot;description&quot;:&quot;A rectangular shape with a flat top and bottom, and straight sides, often symbolizing a document or a sheet of paper in a digital context.&quot;}"></icon></grid-item-label><h3>People's script</h3><p>He wrote in <b>chữ Nôm</b>, the demotic script for Vietnamese, while Literary Chinese carried state prestige.</p></grid-item><grid-item id="UwfIR0HDuB" cell-style="outline" colspan="20"><grid-item-label><icon src="https://iconscdn.pictographic.ai/image/70bnp6n574yd8QViyJZy.svg?stroke=45" source="image.pictographic.icon" alt="interlocking verse rhythm and rhyme" meta="{&quot;description&quot;:&quot;Two interconnected musical notes in a circular formation, symbolizing the concept of rhyme.&quot;}"></icon></grid-item-label><h3>People's meter</h3><p>He chose <b>lục bát</b>, the native six-eight folk form, rather than a Tang-derived court form.</p></grid-item><grid-item id="T4nRda-5wp" cell-style="outline" colspan="20"><grid-item-label><icon src="https://iconscdn.pictographic.ai/image/QULDkvIpc1xlKvmVNK2B.svg?stroke=45" source="image.pictographic.icon" alt="spoken proverb and village conversation" meta="{&quot;description&quot;:&quot;Several small circles connected and form a bigger circle with a small triangle at the bottom, symbolizing a village.&quot;}"></icon></grid-item-label><h3>People's speech</h3><p>Proverbs, idioms, landscapes, and social textures make the work read as Vietnamese despite its Ming setting.</p></grid-item></grid><p role="caption">The poem dates its setting to the Jiajing reign: <i>“Rằng năm Gia Tĩnh triều Minh.”</i> <a href="https://vi.wikisource.org/wiki/Truy%E1%BB%87n_Ki%E1%BB%81u">Vietnamese text</a></p></grid-item></grid></section>
<section image-layout="blank" id="3A6RWd-B7g"><grid spacing="medium"><grid-item id="GmJsQOzH0n" vertical-align="center" colspan="37"><p role="eyebrow">Lines 1–4</p><hr color="accent" thickness="md" width="xs"><blockquote><p font-size="lg"><i>Trăm năm trong cõi người ta,<br>Chữ tài chữ mệnh khéo là ghét nhau.<br>Trải qua một cuộc bể dâu,<br>Những điều trông thấy mà đau đớn lòng.</i></p></blockquote><p>A hundred years in the human realm: <i>tài</i>, talent, and <i>mệnh</i>, destiny, are skilled at hating one another. Having seen a sea become mulberry fields, the poet's heart is hurt.</p></grid-item><grid-item id="EQzi94I6jz" vertical-align="center" colspan="23"><h2>The poem states its thesis in its opening couplets</h2><h4><i>tài mệnh tương đố</i></h4><p>Gifts attract the hostility of fate.</p><h4><i>bể dâu</i></h4><p>Total upheaval. Hearing recent dynastic collapse in the phrase is a critical inference, not documented reception.</p><h4><i>đau đớn lòng</i></h4><p>What the poet has seen hurts. The humanitarian argument begins with that verb.</p><p role="caption"><a href="https://vi.wikisource.org/wiki/Truy%E1%BB%87n_Ki%E1%BB%81u">Text, lines 1–4</a></p></grid-item></grid></section>
<section image-layout="blank" id="KHrL_BV78V" vertical-align="center" background-color="accent"><grid spacing="medium"><grid-item id="otexh5B5YO" vertical-align="center" colspan="18"><display size="lg">III</display></grid-item><grid-item id="DY4YJUxt1H" vertical-align="center" colspan="42"><p role="eyebrow">Fifteen years</p><h1>The story</h1><p font-size="lg">A private vow enters a world where families, bodies, justice, and political legitimacy all have prices.</p></grid-item></grid></section>
<section image-layout="blank" id="P5pCLXvn5X" vertical-align="center"><grid spacing="none"><grid-item id="uP8G0FM_7Q"><h2>The vow, and the price of a daughter</h2><grid marker="number" marker-rule="true" marker-position="above" marker-align="start" marker-numbering-format="decimal-leading-zero" spacing="medium" style="--marker-gap: 0.6em;"><grid-item id="xH8zPCWkfj" colspan="15"><h4>The omen</h4><p>At Đạm Tiên's grave, Kiều mourns a gifted singing-girl whose fate anticipates her own.</p></grid-item><grid-item id="xlbhLxiJyU" colspan="15"><h4>The vow</h4><p>She and Kim Trọng privately pledge marriage before he leaves to mourn an uncle.</p></grid-item><grid-item id="6ADkaTyBP2" colspan="15"><h4>The accusation</h4><p>A false charge threatens her father and brother with prison. The officials want money.</p></grid-item><grid-item id="X1PqtFrkiO" colspan="15"><h4>The sale</h4><p>Kiều sells herself and asks Thúy Vân to keep her vow to Kim. The haggle settles at just over four hundred in gold.</p></grid-item></grid><p role="caption"><i>“Cò kè bớt một thêm hai”</i>: a bit off and a bit on. The daughter becomes the family's negotiable asset.</p></grid-item></grid></section>
<section image-layout="blank" id="khkiQ7Feol" vertical-align="center"><grid spacing="none"><grid-item id="pVrfdQVX3w"><h2>Fifteen years of being bought and sold</h2><grid marker="number" marker-size="large" marker-style="subtle" marker-shape="chevron" marker-position="above" marker-align="center" marker-fill="true" marker-numbering-format="decimal-leading-zero" spacing="none" padding="1em" style="--marker-chip-padding: 0.75em;"><grid-item id="6_672jOYPy" colspan="12"><h4>Mã Giám Sinh</h4><p>A procurer buys, violates, and delivers her to Tú Bà's brothel.</p></grid-item><grid-item id="JzzfjRsuCI" colspan="12"><h4>Sở Khanh</h4><p>A staged elopement and betrayal break her resistance.</p></grid-item><grid-item id="mSh823SQix" colspan="12"><h4>Thúc Sinh</h4><p>He buys her freedom; Hoạn Thư has her abducted and enslaved.</p></grid-item><grid-item id="eX-VBjCgSU" colspan="12"><h4>Second brothel</h4><p>After escape and attempted refuge, she is trafficked again.</p></grid-item><grid-item id="IdbS9V1BGO" colspan="12"><h4>Từ Hải</h4><p>The rebel commander marries her; she holds court and judges her persecutors.</p></grid-item></grid></grid-item></grid></section>
<section image-layout="blank" id="0_oWw4pfbh"><grid spacing="medium"><grid-item id="r62djdQ1w2" vertical-align="center" colspan="25"><p role="eyebrow">The final betrayal</p><h1 font-size="38pt">The state is the last and worst betrayer</h1><hr color="accent" thickness="md" width="xs"><p font-size="lg">Her final ruin is administered by the emperor's lawful representative, not by a pimp or a jealous wife.</p></grid-item><grid-item id="halNeh51_Z" vertical-align="center" colspan="35"><grid divider="sm neutral-border" marker="number" marker-position="inline" marker-numbering-format="decimal-leading-zero" direction="vertical" style="--marker-inline-size: 30pt; --marker-gap: 12pt;"><grid-item id="lzUbdOwrWy" padding="10pt 0"><h4>Amnesty offered</h4><p>Kiều urges Từ Hải to accept Hồ Tôn Hiến's promise of legitimacy.</p></grid-item><grid-item id="hIVUV9JNGr" padding="10pt 0"><h4>Amnesty weaponized</h4><p>The offer is a trap. Từ Hải's forces are attacked and he is killed.</p></grid-item><grid-item id="P1rTdKCXWn" padding="10pt 0"><h4>Victory staged</h4><p>Hồ forces Kiều to perform at his banquet, then marries her off to avoid scandal.</p></grid-item><grid-item id="7Ve6HVPHR-" padding="10pt 0"><h4>Escape attempted</h4><p>She enters the Tiền Đường River; Giác Duyên is waiting with nets.</p></grid-item></grid></grid-item></grid></section>
<section image-layout="blank" id="HPTNAz_dfv"><grid spacing="none"><grid-item id="4iEVWYhs49"><h2>A reunion that refuses to be a happy ending</h2><grid spacing="medium" vertical-sizing="fill"><grid-item id="dbm0rkLyAo" cell-style="subtle" colspan="30"><p role="eyebrow">What is restored</p><h3>Family, vow, ceremony</h3><p>Kim Trọng has married Thúy Vân, supported Kiều's parents, entered office, and continued searching. He finds Kiều with Giác Duyên. The family returns, and the deferred marriage is performed.</p></grid-item><grid-item id="4kkDxZXMk6" background-color="accent" colspan="30"><p role="eyebrow">What remains unrepaired</p><h3>Kiều refuses the marriage bed</h3><p>They live as companions, honoring the youthful vow without consummating it. The refusal is hers. Nguyễn Du devotes <b>526 lines</b> to this settlement and does not explain fifteen years of damage away.</p></grid-item></grid><p role="caption"><b>For discussion:</b> restoration, or an admission that restitution cannot reverse experience?</p></grid-item></grid></section>
<section image-layout="blank" id="xVh1xSK4ZB" vertical-align="center" background-color="accent"><grid spacing="medium"><grid-item id="mxAlgFm7Xn" vertical-align="center" colspan="18"><display size="lg">IV</display></grid-item><grid-item id="OCMEa4d_kE" vertical-align="center" colspan="42"><p role="eyebrow">Reading the poem's claims</p><h1>The two values</h1><p font-size="lg">Its realism follows institutions and money. Its humanitarian force follows intention under coercion.</p></grid-item></grid></section>
<section image-layout="blank" id="qZ5BcdoB4J"><grid spacing="medium"><grid-item id="q69UoYDA4i" vertical-align="center" colspan="36"><h2>Textual detail—not summary—builds Thúy Kiều</h2><grid spacing="small"><grid-item id="CoW36F-jf5" cell-style="subtle" colspan="30"><h4>Lines 29–32</h4><p>Poetry, painting, song, the five-note scale, and mastery of the <i>hồ cầm</i>.</p></grid-item><grid-item id="pjSDS-9MC6" cell-style="subtle" colspan="30"><h4>Line 34</h4><p>Her composition, <i>Bạc mệnh</i> (“thin destiny”), grieves whoever hears it.</p></grid-item><grid-item id="V0w9Rme7BM" cell-style="subtle" colspan="30"><h4>Line 26</h4><p><i>“Hoa ghen thua thắm, liễu hờn kém xanh”</i>: flowers envy her color; willows resent her green.</p></grid-item><grid-item id="Ti6mRwSLwN" cell-style="subtle" colspan="30"><h4>The moral bind</h4><p><i>hiếu</i> (filial duty) collides with <i>tình</i> (her vow to Kim). She reasons, errs, then counsels Từ Hải’s fatal surrender.</p></grid-item></grid></grid-item><grid-item id="ubprRA878u" padding="0" colspan="24"><img src="https://cdn-staging.gamma.app/QWjS6fBfpt/generated-images/n5gIqCBRFIEzZPHNOTxZ8.png" saved-media-id="t1wrhg2iph3x63o" source="image.ai-generated" fill="true" image-style="vietnamese-manuscript-editorial" alt="Ink-and-opaque-pigment editorial illustration on warm dó-paper-like fibers, an interpretive non-documentary figure of Thúy Kiều seated with a hồ cầm, flowering branch and willow leaves pressing inward from opposite edges, a vermilion thread tightening around the available space, lampblack, old gold and indigo, Vietnamese manuscript and woodblock conventions, no text or lettering" meta="{&quot;width&quot;:1248,&quot;height&quot;:1664}"></grid-item></grid></section>
<section image-layout="blank" id="O-xC0HHpdR" vertical-align="center"><grid spacing="none"><grid-item id="vKKe-LJHki"><h2>Realistic value: every turn of the plot is a transaction</h2><p font-size="lg"><i>“Trong tay đã sẵn đồng tiền / Dầu lòng đổi trắng thay đen khó gì”</i><br>With money in hand, turning white into black is no hard thing.</p><grid marker="number" marker-size="large" marker-style="subtle" marker-shape="chevron" marker-position="above" marker-align="center" marker-fill="true" marker-numbering-format="decimal-leading-zero" spacing="none" padding="1em" style="--marker-chip-padding: 0.75em;"><grid-item id="xXdH9n-8oq" colspan="15"><h4>Extortion</h4><p>Money ruins her father through purchasable justice.</p></grid-item><grid-item id="aqdgFSAoGc" colspan="15"><h4>Purchase</h4><p>A negotiated price converts Kiều into property.</p></grid-item><grid-item id="sm-BRU9lSa" colspan="15"><h4>Repurchase</h4><p>Thúc Sinh's money frees her from the first brothel.</p></grid-item><grid-item id="uJ-d6geLWG" colspan="15"><h4>Official calculation</h4><p>Hồ Tôn Hiến's political bargain kills her husband.</p></grid-item></grid><p role="caption">Courts, merchants, and the imperial commission are all shown as purchasable institutions.</p></grid-item></grid></section>
<section image-layout="blank" id="hGL_cv-hcc"><grid spacing="medium"><grid-item id="PxqKw6r-Zj" background-color="accent" vertical-align="center" colspan="24"><p role="eyebrow">Lines 3251–3252</p><display size="md">tâm outweighs tài</display><p font-size="lg"><i>“Thiện căn ở tại lòng ta / Chữ tâm kia mới bằng ba chữ tài”</i></p><p>The root of good lies in our own heart; <i>tâm</i> is worth three times <i>tài</i>.</p></grid-item><grid-item id="gzdyUjc1Yy" vertical-align="center" colspan="36"><h2>Humanitarian value: he defends a woman his society would condemn</h2><p>Neo-Confucian orthodoxy judged women by <b>chữ trinh</b>, chastity. The poem answers that virtue lies in intention under coercion. Kiều sold herself for her father and held her vow inwardly despite being trafficked twice.</p><p>Its sympathy also reaches Đạm Tiên, the outlawed Từ Hải, and even Hoạn Thư, whose defense is persuasive enough that Kiều releases her.</p><hr color="accent" thickness="md" width="sm"><p role="caption">Lines 3247–3248 sharpen the argument through sound: <i>tài</i>, talent, rhymes with <i>tai</i>, disaster.</p></grid-item></grid></section>
<section image-layout="blank" id="UsiVm16DbE" vertical-align="center" background-color="accent"><grid spacing="medium"><grid-item id="SMQJQQZ2y1" vertical-align="center" colspan="18"><display size="lg">V</display></grid-item><grid-item id="b9WJ2HZQFH" vertical-align="center" colspan="42"><p role="eyebrow">Sound as argument</p><h1>The art of lục bát</h1><p font-size="lg">A six-eight folk form links each couplet to the next through rhyme, tone, and memory.</p></grid-item></grid></section>
<section image-layout="blank" id="tyPa9z4f5l"><grid spacing="none"><grid-item id="EnVn2RufhS"><h2>How the six-eight line works, in the lines we just read</h2><p role="subheading">Each editable tile is one syllable. Vermilion marks the waist rhyme linking the six-line to the sixth syllable of the eight-line.</p><freeform-block w="840" h="300"><box type="content" y="32" w="92" h="46" vertical-align="center" sizing="fixed" background-color="palette-5" style="padding: 6pt;"><p font-size="13pt" align="center"><b>6 syllables</b></p></box><box type="content" x="210" y="32" w="78" h="46" vertical-align="center" sizing="fixed" background-color="surface" style="padding: 6pt;"><p align="center">Trăm</p></box><box type="content" x="310" y="32" w="78" h="46" vertical-align="center" sizing="fixed" background-color="surface" style="padding: 6pt;"><p align="center">năm</p></box><box type="content" x="410" y="32" w="78" h="46" vertical-align="center" sizing="fixed" background-color="surface" style="padding: 6pt;"><p align="center">trong</p></box><box type="content" x="510" y="32" w="78" h="46" vertical-align="center" sizing="fixed" background-color="surface" style="padding: 6pt;"><p align="center">cõi</p></box><box type="content" x="610" y="32" w="78" h="46" vertical-align="center" sizing="fixed" background-color="surface" style="padding: 6pt;"><p align="center">người</p></box><box type="content" x="710" y="32" w="78" h="46" vertical-align="center" sizing="fixed" background-color="accent" style="padding: 6pt;"><p align="center"><b>ta</b></p></box><box type="content" y="118" w="92" h="46" vertical-align="center" sizing="fixed" background-color="palette-5" style="padding: 6pt;"><p font-size="13pt" align="center"><b>8 syllables</b></p></box><box type="content" x="105" y="118" w="78" h="46" vertical-align="center" sizing="fixed" background-color="surface" style="padding: 6pt;"><p align="center">Chữ</p></box><box type="content" x="195" y="118" w="78" h="46" vertical-align="center" sizing="fixed" background-color="surface" style="padding: 6pt;"><p align="center"><b>tài</b></p></box><box type="content" x="285" y="118" w="78" h="46" vertical-align="center" sizing="fixed" background-color="surface" style="padding: 6pt;"><p align="center">chữ</p></box><box type="content" x="375" y="118" w="78" h="46" vertical-align="center" sizing="fixed" background-color="surface" style="padding: 6pt;"><p align="center"><b>mệnh</b></p></box><box type="content" x="465" y="118" w="78" h="46" vertical-align="center" sizing="fixed" background-color="surface" style="padding: 6pt;"><p align="center">khéo</p></box><box type="content" x="555" y="118" w="78" h="46" vertical-align="center" sizing="fixed" background-color="accent" style="padding: 6pt;"><p align="center"><b>là</b></p></box><box type="content" x="645" y="118" w="78" h="46" vertical-align="center" sizing="fixed" background-color="surface" style="padding: 6pt;"><p align="center">ghét</p></box><box type="content" x="735" y="118" w="78" h="46" vertical-align="center" sizing="fixed" background-color="surface" style="padding: 6pt;"><p align="center">nhau</p></box><box type="content" x="618" y="84" w="108"><p font-size="13pt" align="center"><span text-color="accent"><b>ta </b></span>↘<span text-color="accent"><b> là</b></span></p></box><box type="content" x="30" y="205" w="370" h="68" sizing="fixed" background-color="surface" style="padding: 10pt 14pt;"><p font-size="13pt"><b>Chain rhyme:</b> <span text-color="accent">nhau → dâu → đau</span>; then <span text-color="accent">lòng → phong → hồng</span>.</p></box><box type="content" x="430" y="205" w="380" h="68" sizing="fixed" background-color="surface" style="padding: 10pt 14pt;"><p font-size="13pt"><b>Tone rule:</b> positions 2, 4, 6 run bằng, trắc, bằng. <i>là</i> and <i>nhau</i> are both bằng but use different tones.</p></box></freeform-block><p role="caption">Kiều contains 1,627 six-eight couplets. <a href="https://vi.wikisource.org/wiki/Truy%E1%BB%87n_Ki%E1%BB%81u">Text, lines 1–6</a></p></grid-item></grid></section>
<section image-layout="blank" id="mJqNBRqXno" vertical-align="center"><grid spacing="none"><grid-item id="9SNtZul7pJ"><h2>Why the form suits this story</h2><grid marker="number" marker-rule="true" marker-position="above" marker-align="start" marker-numbering-format="decimal-leading-zero" spacing="medium" style="--marker-gap: 0.6em;"><grid-item id="Emvxj0OGaE" colspan="15"><h4>Folk register</h4><p>Lục bát is the meter of ca dao and lullabies, composed and enjoyed across social classes.</p></grid-item><grid-item id="MTv4rd5fdy" colspan="15"><h4>Interlocking rhyme</h4><p>Each couplet passes a sound forward instead of closing in isolation.</p></grid-item><grid-item id="5o80uvL_qW" colspan="15"><h4>Narrative pressure</h4><p>On this reading, the unbroken hand-off suits a life sliding from one disaster into the next.</p></grid-item><grid-item id="Lt7Koenj3n" colspan="15"><h4>Memory</h4><p>The chain-rhymed pattern supports recitation across a narrative of 3,254 lines.</p></grid-item></grid><p role="caption">The poem entered the same rhythmic register as songs its audience already knew.</p></grid-item></grid></section>
<section image-layout="blank" id="vDS4S8waFx"><grid spacing="none"><grid-item id="d75Hvg4rlt"><h2>What English cannot carry: four translators, one opening</h2><table col-widths="[20,20,60]" header-row="true" borders="rows" striped="false"><tbody><tr><td><p>Translator</p></td><td><p>Governing choice</p></td><td><p>Opening decision</p></td></tr><tr><td><p><b>Vladislav Zhukov</b><br>2004</p></td><td><p>Formal meter</p></td><td><p><i>“Were full five-score the years allotted to born man”</i></p></td></tr><tr><td><p><b>Timothy Allen</b><br>2019</p></td><td><p>Colloquial voice</p></td><td><p><i>“It's an old story: good luck and good looks / don't always mix.”</i></p></td></tr><tr><td><p><b>Nguyễn Bình</b><br>2021</p></td><td><p>Heroic couplet</p></td><td><p><i>“'Tween Fate and Talent hatred seems to reign.”</i></p></td></tr><tr><td><p><b>Huỳnh Sanh Thông</b><br>1983</p></td><td><p>Blank verse</p></td><td><p>The standard scholarly English version; one of translations into roughly twenty languages.</p></td></tr></tbody></table><p role="caption">No English meter reproduces a tonal waist rhyme. Each version relinquishes some combination of music, compression, and plainness.</p></grid-item></grid></section>
<section image-layout="blank" id="uVbke8PGW-"><grid spacing="none"><grid-item id="w00UARCpZA"><h2>The afterlife of a poem</h2><p>Kiều moved into cải lương and chèo opera, painting, Western-style opera, and the 1924 film <i>Kim Vân Kiều</i>. It also became political and diplomatic language.</p><smart-layout variant="minimalTimeline" orientation="horizontal" cell-size="20"><smart-layout-item><h4>2000 · Clinton</h4><p>In Hanoi, he quotes the seasonal turn from lotus to chrysanthemum, winter to spring.</p></smart-layout-item><smart-layout-item><h4>2015 · Biden</h4><p>At a lunch for Nguyễn Phú Trọng, the Vice President quotes mist clearing and clouds parting.</p></smart-layout-item><smart-layout-item><h4>2015 · Commemoration</h4><p>Vietnam marks Nguyễn Du's 250th birth anniversary nationally, with UNESCO taking part.</p></smart-layout-item><smart-layout-item><h4>2016 · Obama</h4><p>Another American president addresses Vietnamese counterparts through Kiều in Hanoi.</p></smart-layout-item></smart-layout><p role="caption">Reported English renderings on these occasions draw on Huỳnh Sanh Thông. <a href="https://nguyendu.com.vn/m/vi/tong-thong-my-lay-kieu-qua-ban-dich-nao--33F1C684D865596DB82A31C0E3BEFA31.html">Nguyễn Du memorial site</a></p></grid-item></grid></section>
<section image-layout="blank" id="SeaLsvg_yr" background-color="heading"><grid spacing="none"><grid-item id="ssnxWGm_8w" vertical-align="center" colspan="38"><p role="eyebrow">Lines 3253–3254</p><h1 font-size="38pt">Nguyễn Du expected to be forgotten</h1><blockquote><p font-size="lg"><i>“Lời quê chắp nhặt dông dài<br>Mua vui cũng được một vài trống canh”</i></p></blockquote><p>Rustic words strung together at length, good for a few hours' amusement.</p><hr color="accent" thickness="md" width="xs"><p>The modesty was conventional; the estimate was wrong. Nguyễn Du inherited a plot and supplied a consciousness, wrote in the people's script and meter, and held that a woman sold twice into a brothel had kept her honor.</p><p font-size="lg"><b>The claim that remains plain: tâm outweighs tài.</b></p></grid-item><grid-item id="DjHfr1xK73" padding="0" colspan="22"><img src="https://cdn-staging.gamma.app/QWjS6fBfpt/generated-images/EFK1liRa7RPZKUX7nzsRV.png" saved-media-id="xoud88gjw4o04wp" source="image.ai-generated" fill="true" image-style="vietnamese-manuscript-editorial" alt="Ink-and-opaque-pigment editorial illustration on warm dó-paper-like fibers, an open manuscript folio without legible writing beside a quiet river threshold, a single vermilion thread leaving the page and continuing unresolved beyond the upper edge, lampblack, old gold and indigo under soft window light, Vietnamese chữ Nôm manuscript and woodblock conventions, no text or lettering" meta="{&quot;width&quot;:1248,&quot;height&quot;:1664}"></grid-item></grid></section>